<SddAmplifyObservability keywords="observability, amplify, logs, metrics, traces, alerts, slo, dashboards, sdd-amplify-observability" type="directive" ver="2.0">
  <Mission>
    Make observability a set of design decisions in a scope spec under discovery — logs, metrics,
    traces, alerts — instead of an afterthought sprinkled at execution time. Loaded lazily by the
    discovery interview's triage when the scope has an operational runtime (service, worker,
    long-lived process); inherits the session core — not repeated here.

    Input — the scope spec draft + interview context. Output — an `Observability` subsection
    inside Requirements & Constraints of the scope spec + follow-up items on the discovery
    interview map. Out of scope: dashboard layouts, vendor configuration — the spec records what
    is observed and why, tooling carries the how.
  </Mission>

  <BeliefState deps="AX_OPERATOR_LANGUAGE, AX_OPERATOR_SAFEGUARD, AX_NO_PROCESS_NARRATION">
    {{> "axiom/process/ax-amplify-defaults-first"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-decision-log-required"}}

    {{> "axiom/logging/ax-structured-logging"}}

    {{> "axiom/logging/ax-log-density"}}

    {{> "axiom/logging/ax-alerts-on-symptoms"}}
  </BeliefState>

  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NO_RUNTIME_SURFACE` | Triage misfired: no operational runtime (pure library — observability belongs to the consumer) — report and return control |
    | `H_OPERATOR_REJECTS_DEFAULTS` | Operator declines the whole defaults package and skips deep-dive — leave the spec untouched |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_PROPOSE_DEFAULTS">
      <Goal>Assemble the observability defaults package for this product class.</Goal>
      <Action>
        From the spec draft, list the operational surfaces: entry points, external I/O, queues,
        long operations. No runtime surface → `H_NO_RUNTIME_SURFACE`. Per
        `AX_AMPLIFY_DEFAULTS_FIRST`, draft one default decision per signal: logs (structure +
        levels per `AX_STRUCTURED_LOGGING`, density per `AX_LOG_DENSITY`), metrics (RED for
        request paths / USE for resources — the minimal set answering «жив ли сервис и где
        болит»), traces (propagation boundaries + sampling), alerts (symptom → threshold →
        severity → first action, per `AX_ALERTS_ON_SYMPTOMS`) — grounded in what live products of
        this class ship; short targeted research when class practice is uncertain.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_AGREE">
      <Goal>One accept-or-edit gate; deep-dive only on explicit pick.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Present the package as ONE reply per `AX_AMPLIFY_DEFAULTS_FIRST` (AskUserQuestion when
        available, else `QUESTION_FORMAT`); each signal accept / edit / deep-dive. Deep-dive topic
        map: logs → metrics → traces → alerts → SLO linkage. Untouched signals keep their
        defaults. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_APPLY">
      <Goal>Write the agreed observability decisions into the spec.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Write an `### Observability` subsection into Requirements & Constraints of the scope spec:
        **Logs** (структура, уровни, транспорт) → **Metrics** (`| Метрика | Тип | Что отвечает |`)
        → **Traces** (границы propagation, sampling) → **Alerts**
        (`| Симптом | Порог | Severity | Первое действие |`). Non-default picks and notable
        accepted defaults → Decision Log per `AX_DECISION_LOG_REQUIRED`. Unresolved topics → items
        on the discovery interview map. Return control to the interview.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

  <ChatOutput>
    {{> "contract/process/question-format"}}

    Service line — dim, internal, never narrated (`AX_NO_PROCESS_NARRATION`):
    `📡 AMP_OBS · signals=<n> · accepted=<n> · edited=<n> · dive=<n>`.
  </ChatOutput>
</SddAmplifyObservability>
